---
// The Lumit wordmark, rebuilt from the After Effects reference.
//
// Each keyframe is TWO rounded rectangles sharing a corner at ninety degrees —
// the construction the AE project uses (ADBE Vector Rect Size and Rect Roundness
// both animated). Wide arms overlap into the icon's diamond; narrow them and the
// chevron opens; redistribute their lengths and square the corners and it is the
// letter. No path morphing: thickness, arm split and corner radius do all of it.
//
// Position, thickness and the white core are sampled off the render itself rather
// than eased by hand, so the motion is the reference's, not an impression of it.
// Measured: thickness 30.9 -> 13.6, arms equal at rest (55.9 each) splitting to
// 70.3 / 47.0, travel x 114.5 -> -44.1 -> 21.4, white gone by frame 40.
//
// The t is the L turned 180 degrees; the i's tittle is a small diamond.
//
// Driven from script: geometry attributes are not reliably animatable in CSS on
// iOS. Without script, or under reduced motion, the markup is the finished
// wordmark standing still.
interface Props { class?: string }
const { class: klass } = Astro.props;
---

